.TH "CPM" "1" "September 2026" "cpm 0.10.0" "Code Project Maturity"
.SH NAME
cpm \- code project maturity: quality gate, rule engine, and project
scaffolding
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]cpm\f[R] \f[I]command\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]cpm\f[R] is a fast, self\-contained code\-project\-maturity tool.
It runs a tiered quality gate (format, lint, test, SAST), a
fuzzy/AST\-aware rule engine over a bundled rule corpus, and project
scaffolding and reporting helpers.
.PP
Output is designed to be accessible: findings are emitted as clickable
\f[I]file:line\f[R] references, and this man page provides a
screen\-reader\-friendly alternative to \f[B]\(enhelp\f[R].
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Project lifecycle
.TP
\f[B]new\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]
Create a new project.
Convention: \f[I]\-\-\-\f[R]
(e.g.\ \f[CR]code\-cpp\-vulnerability\-scan\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]new test\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]
Add a new test file (e.g.\ \f[CR]cpm new test parser\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]new module\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]
Add a module (\f[CR]src/name.cpp\f[R] + \f[CR]src/name.hpp\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]init\f[R]
Create a new \f[CR]cpm.toml\f[R] in the current directory.
.TP
\f[B]install\f[R]
Install tools declared in \f[CR]cpm.toml\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]uninstall\f[R] [\f[B]\(enall\f[R]]
Remove cpm from PATH.
With \f[B]\(enall\f[R], also remove installed tools.
.TP
\f[B]eject\f[R]
Generate a \f[CR]Makefile\f[R] and \f[CR]CMakeLists.txt\f[R].
.SS Quality gate
.TP
\f[B]check\f[R] [\f[B]\(enfast\f[R]|\f[B]\(enfull\f[R]]
Run the tiered quality gate.
\f[B]\(enfast\f[R] runs the quickest tier only; \f[B]\(enfull\f[R] runs
every tier.
.TP
\f[B]lint\f[R]
Run all lint checks.
.TP
\f[B]format\f[R]
Auto\-format all files.
.TP
\f[B]build\f[R]
Build the project.
.TP
\f[B]run\f[R]
Build and run the project.
.TP
\f[B]test\f[R]
Run tests.
.TP
\f[B]coverage\f[R] [\f[B]\(ensonar\f[R]]
Build with coverage and report.
\f[B]\(ensonar\f[R] emits XML.
.TP
\f[B]clean\f[R]
Remove build artifacts.
.TP
\f[B]audit\f[R]
Check installed tool versions against \f[CR]cpm.toml\f[R].
.SS Rules, findings and reporting
.TP
\f[B]scan\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]
Scan one or more repositories for quality metrics and rule findings.
.TP
\f[B]score\f[R]
Show the maturity score (0\-100) and badge.
.TP
\f[B]findings\f[R] [\f[I]repo\f[R]]
Query findings.
Options: \f[B]\(enseverity\f[R] \f[I]level\f[R], \f[B]\(enjunit\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]report\f[R]
Generate a report from recorded findings.
.TP
\f[B]xref\f[R]
Validate all cross\-references.
.TP
\f[B]todo\f[R]
Show TODO/FIXME items collected by the scraper.
.SS Version and configuration
.TP
\f[B]version\f[R] [\f[I]part\f[R]]
Show the version, or bump it (\f[I]part\f[R] = major|minor|patch).
.TP
\f[B]bump\f[R] \f[I]part\f[R]
Bump the version (major|minor|patch).
.TP
\f[B]tools\f[R]
Show installed tool versions.
.TP
\f[B]get\f[R] [\f[I]key\f[R]]
Show configuration (all values, or a specific \f[I]key\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]set\f[R] \f[I]key\f[R] \f[I]value\f[R]
Update a configuration value.
.TP
\f[B]sort\f[R] \f[I]op\f[R]
Canonical sort (\f[B]check\f[R]|\f[B]fix\f[R]) for cpm\-toml,
ts\-imports, or lines.
.TP
\f[B]docs index\f[R] [\f[I]dir\f[R]] [\f[B]\(encheck\f[R]]
Generate a Markdown index of a docs directory.
\f[B]\(encheck\f[R] verifies it is up to date without writing.
.SS Git integration
.TP
\f[B]hook\f[R]
Install git hooks for the current repository.
.TP
\f[B]hook \(englobal\f[R]
Install global pre\-commit security hooks.
.TP
\f[B]hook \(englobal \(encheck\f[R]
Verify global hook health.
.TP
\f[B]hook \(englobal \(enstatus\f[R]
Show which checks are enabled or disabled.
.TP
\f[B]hook \(englobal \(enenable\f[R] \f[I]check\f[R]
Enable a specific check.
.TP
\f[B]hook \(englobal \(endisable\f[R] \f[I]check\f[R]
Disable a specific check.
.TP
\f[B]hook \(englobal \(enremove\f[R]
Remove the global hooks.
.TP
\f[B]unhook\f[R]
Remove per\-repository git hooks.
.TP
\f[B]commit\f[R]
Interactive Conventional Commit helper.
.TP
\f[B]issue\f[R] [\f[I]title\f[R]]
Local\-first issue tracking (push/pull to GitHub).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Success, or no blocking findings.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
One or more blocking (error\-severity) findings, or a command failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]cpm.toml\f[R]
Per\-project configuration (tools, version, check settings).
.TP
\f[I].config/.pii\f[R], \f[I]\(ti/.local/share/pii/patterns.d/*.pii\f[R]
PII detection pattern sources for the PII check.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the fast quality gate in the current repository:
.IP
.EX
cpm check \-\-fast
.EE
.PP
Scan a directory tree and show the maturity score:
.IP
.EX
cpm scan . && cpm score
.EE
.PP
Query only error\-severity findings as JUnit XML:
.IP
.EX
cpm findings \-\-severity error \-\-junit
.EE
